From: TB-X606V kernel project
Subject: [PATCH] ram_console: use the Kconfig SRAM window, not the misparsed DT node

The shipping bootloader passes a ram_console DT node this 4.9.117 driver misreads, ioremap fails, ram_console_buffer
stays NULL while ram_console_buffer_pa is garbage, and fiq_cache_init, mtk_cpuidle_init and mcdi_enter oops.
Use CONFIG_MTK_RAM_CONSOLE_ADDR/SIZE (0x10DC00/0x800, what the shipping kernel logs) and keep _pa NULL on failure.

---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/ram_console/mtk_ram_console.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/ram_console/mtk_ram_console.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/ram_console/mtk_ram_console.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/ram_console/mtk_ram_console.c
@@ -672,15 +672,19 @@
 	struct mem_desc_t sram = { 0 };
 
 	if (of_scan_flat_dt(dt_get_ram_console, &sram)) {
-		if (sram.start == 0) {
-			sram.start = CONFIG_MTK_RAM_CONSOLE_ADDR;
-			sram.size = CONFIG_MTK_RAM_CONSOLE_SIZE;
-		}
+		/*
+		 * The bootloader of the shipping 4.9.190 firmware hands over a ram_console DT node this driver
+		 * misparses (0xac000000001@0x8000010dc00). Its own log shows the real window is the Kconfig one.
+		 */
+		sram.start = CONFIG_MTK_RAM_CONSOLE_ADDR;
+		sram.size = CONFIG_MTK_RAM_CONSOLE_SIZE;
 		bufp = ioremap_wc(sram.start, sram.size);
 		ram_console_buffer_pa = (struct ram_console_buffer *)sram.start;
 		if (bufp)
 			buffer_size = sram.size;
 		else {
+			/* keep the _pa helpers' NULL checks truthful: they also dereference ram_console_buffer */
+			ram_console_buffer_pa = NULL;
 			pr_err("ram_console: ioremap failed, [0x%lx, 0x%lx]\n",
 					sram.start,
 			       sram.size);
